Band Description

Mandible Relay Office is a five-member acoustic-electronic ensemble built around the principle that rhythm can continue after the visible gesture that created it has ended.

Lucía Barragán — quijada, palm and knuckle strikes, damping control, tooth-line articulation, After-Rattle Window design.

Erik Voss — minimal-techno drums, mono sub, mute architecture, filter automation, structural silence.

Daniela Cruz — prepared Wurlitzer, clipped dyads, damped tine attacks, harmonic resets.

Mateo Salgado — clay udu, cavity percussion, low machine-hit substitution, muted shell taps.

Clara Weiss — bass flute, breath pedals, key noise, low-air entrances, narrow descending intervals.

There is no conventional frontperson. Lucía creates the physical event and its unpredictable after-motion; Erik determines how much machine rhythm is removed around that decay; Daniela frames impact and clear points with short fixed-pitch harmony; Mateo replaces selected synthetic low hits with clay resonance; Clara occupies the clean windows after the final tooth clicks. Live versions vary because tooth looseness, grip position, bone dryness, impact force, and room temperature alter the length and shape of every after-rattle.

