Track 3: Dispatch Ends When the Jaw Stops Moving

Story & Context: The closer runs at 120 BPM and begins without sub. Lucía plays widely spaced quijada strikes, each followed by a full CLEAR window of at least one beat. Erik uses only kick and one muted hat pulse. Daniela plays no chords for the opening section. Mateo places a single open udu bass tone every eight beats, always after CLEAR. Clara sustains one low bass-flute octave through an entire four-bar passage, then cuts it before the next strike so the quijada can own the spectrum again. In the final minute, electronic elements disappear one at a time: hats, Wurlitzer, udu, then kick. Lucía makes one final medium-strength strike. The loose teeth chatter, thin to two isolated clicks, and stop. No sub, voice, field recording, or reverberant tail follows. The recording ends on the first instant of genuine silence after the jaw has fully stopped.

